import {advanced,brief} from './advanced.js';
export default [
advanced('B2',1,{t:'Aspect: natija va jarayonni tanlash',goal:'Ish natijasi va vaqt davomida kechgan jarayonni aniq farqlaysiz.',context:'Mahalla kutubxonasini yangilash loyihasi.',rules:['Perfect simple tugallangan natija yoki miqdorga, perfect continuous esa jarayon va davomiylikka e’tibor beradi.','I have painted three walls va I have been painting walls bir vaziyatning turli tomonlarini ko‘rsatadi.','For ikki shaklda ham kelishi mumkin; shaklni faqat vaqt so‘ziga qarab tanlamang.'],pattern:'have completed / have been working',ex:['We have repaired three shelves.','We have been repairing shelves all morning.','She has known the manager for years.','I have been checking the labels.','The team has collected enough books.','How many labels have you checked?'],v:['outcome|yakuniy natija|/ˈaʊtkʌm/|a measurable outcome','ongoing|davom etayotgan|/ˈɒnɡəʊɪŋ/|ongoing work','estimate|taxminiy baho|/ˈestɪmət/|a time estimate','evidence|dalil|/ˈevɪdəns/|clear evidence'],read:'The library team has repaired three shelves, but the work has taken longer than expected. Volunteers have been checking damaged books all morning. A photograph of the busy room shows effort, yet it does not tell us how many books can safely return to the shelves. The manager therefore records both time spent and usable results. One volunteer argues that only completed work matters. Another points out that checking an unsafe shelf can prevent an accident even if no new shelf is finished. Both views are reasonable, but neither is sufficient alone. A progress report should explain what has been completed, what is still being investigated, and why the remaining work is necessary. The team’s next estimate will include inspection time instead of treating it as a delay with no value.',rq:[['Muallif nimani tavsiya qiladi?','record both effort and usable results','count only finished shelves','use photographs instead of records','Har ikki o‘lchov maqsad uchun zarur.'],['Inspection qanday baholanadi?','valuable even without a finished shelf','always a waste','proof that all shelves are safe','Tekshiruv xavfni aniqlaydi.']],listen:'Manager: We have repaired three shelves. Volunteer: We have been checking books for four hours. Manager: That work matters, but we need to record which books are safe. Volunteer: Then the report should show both the completed repairs and the inspection still in progress.',lq:[['Qancha vaqt tekshirildi?','four hours','three hours','four days','Four hours.'],['Hisobotda nima bo‘lsin?','results and ongoing inspection','only a photo','only delays','Ikki jihat ham aytiladi.']],table:[['Tokchalar','three'],['Tekshiruv vaqti','four hours']],fill:[['We have ___ three shelves. (repair)','repaired'],['We have been ___ all morning. (work)','working'],['She has ___ him for years. (know)','known']],fix:['We have been knowing the manager for years.','We have known the manager for years.'],mc:['Miqdorga e’tibor qaysi?','We have checked twenty books.','We have been checking books.','We are checking books.','Twenty tugallangan miqdor.'],task:'Progress report yozing: tugallangan ish, davom etgan jarayon, dalil va keyingi vaqt taxmini.',model:'Our team has repaired three shelves and returned twenty books to use. We have been checking the remaining books since Monday, and some need further inspection. The work has taken longer than we expected because checking safety is part of the task, rather than an unnecessary delay. A photograph shows that volunteers are busy, but it cannot replace a record of usable results. We recommend recording both completed repairs and inspection time. This will help the next team estimate the remaining work more accurately. We should also explain why an unfinished inspection may still be valuable: it can prevent an unsafe bookcase from returning to use.',speak:'Ishga ketgan vaqt natijaga teng emas degan fikrni dalil bilan muhokama qiling.',transform:['Jarayonga urg‘u bering: We started checking books four hours ago and are still checking them.','We have been checking books for four hours.'],structure:['The report needs two measures.','Three shelves are repaired, and inspection continues.','Results and effort answer different questions.'],visual:'timeline'}),
advanced('B2',2,{t:'Future Continuous va Future Perfect',goal:'Kelajakdagi davom etadigan ishni o‘sha paytgacha tugaydigan natijadan ajratasiz.',context:'Maktab ko‘rgazmasi uchun muddatlar.',rules:['Will be + -ing kelajakdagi bir vaqtda davom etayotgan ishni ko‘rsatadi.','Will have + V3 kelajak nuqtasigacha tugallangan natijani bildiradi.','By Friday — juma kelguncha; at ten — o‘n paytida. Muddat real reja bilan mos bo‘lsin.'],pattern:'at ten: will be preparing / by ten: will have prepared',ex:['At ten we will be arranging the displays.','By noon we will have finished the labels.','Will you be using the projector?','The guests will be arriving at two.','We will have checked the cables by then.','The team will not have finished by nine.'],v:['deadline|yakuniy muddat|/ˈdedlaɪn/|meet a deadline','schedule|jadval|/ˈʃedjuːl/|a realistic schedule','display|ko‘rgazma|/dɪˈspleɪ/|arrange a display','by then|o‘sha paytgacha|/baɪ ðen/|completed by then'],read:'The exhibition opens at two, but preparation continues through the morning. At ten, one group will be arranging the displays while another checks the projector. By noon, they will have finished the labels. This does not mean that the whole room will be ready at noon: cables still need checking. The organiser asks everyone to state both their activity and the result promised by a deadline. Last year, a team said it would be working on the posters at eleven. Other groups mistakenly understood this as a promise that the posters would be finished by eleven. The new schedule avoids that confusion. It also includes a buffer before visitors arrive. A timetable is useful only when people agree on what each time refers to and what evidence will show that a task is complete.',rq:[['Nega yangi jadval ikki narsani ajratadi?','activity time and completion deadline were confused','visitors arrive at noon','labels need no work','Davom va yakun vaqtini chalkashtirishgan.'],['Noonda xona tayyormi?','not necessarily','definitely','never','Labels tugashi barcha vazifa tugashi emas.']],listen:'At ten we will be arranging the displays. By noon we will have finished the labels, but we still need thirty minutes to check the cables. Visitors arrive at two. Please do not treat the label deadline as the completion time for the whole room.',lq:[['Cables uchun vaqt?','thirty minutes','two hours','ten minutes','Thirty minutes.'],['Mehmonlar qachon?','two','noon','ten','Arrive at two.']],table:[['Labels muddati','noon'],['Cable tekshiruvi','thirty minutes']],fill:[['At ten we will be ___ displays. (arrange)','arranging'],['By noon we will have ___ labels. (finish)','finished'],['Will you be ___ the projector? (use)','using']],fix:['By noon we will have finish the labels.','By noon we will have finished the labels.'],mc:['Noongacha tugashni bildiruvchi gap?','We will have finished by noon.','We will be working at noon.','We worked at noon.','Future Perfect tugallanish.'],task:'Ko‘rgazma uchun davom etuvchi vazifa va yakuniy muddatlari ajratilgan email yozing.',model:'Dear team, at ten we will be arranging the displays and testing the projector. By noon, we will have finished the labels. However, the room will not be fully ready until the cables have been checked. We have allowed thirty minutes for that task and a further buffer before visitors arrive at two. Please distinguish an activity in progress from a result promised by a deadline. If your group expects a delay, tell us which result will be affected rather than simply saying that you will still be busy. This will allow the other groups to adjust their plans without misunderstanding the schedule.',speak:'Ikki guruhning vaqt jadvalini kelishtiring; by va at farqini aniqlashtiring.',transform:['By noon tugallanish: We plan to finish the labels before noon.','We will have finished the labels by noon.'],structure:['The schedule separates activity and completion.','Labels finish by noon; cables need another thirty minutes.','The room deadline is later than the label deadline.'],visual:'timeline'}),
advanced('B2',3,{t:'Third Conditional: bo‘lmagan o‘tmish',goal:'O‘tmishdagi tanlovning muqobil natijasini dalildan ajratib aytasiz.',context:'Sayohat rejasidan saboq olish.',rules:['If + had + V3, would have + V3 sodir bo‘lmagan o‘tmishning taxminiy natijasi.','Would if qismida odatiy third conditional shakli emas.','Muqobil natija taxmin: haqiqiy tarix sifatida aytmang; could yoki might ehtimolni o‘zgartiradi.'],pattern:'If we had checked, we would have noticed.',ex:['If we had checked the timetable, we would have noticed the change.','We would have arrived earlier if we had left at eight.','If I had asked, she might have helped.','They could have waited if they had known.','Had we planned better, we would have saved time.','The trip would not have failed if the bus had arrived.'],v:['alternative|muqobil|/ɔːlˈtɜːnətɪv/|an alternative outcome','overlook|e’tibordan qochirmoq|/ˌəʊvəˈlʊk/|overlook a change','regret|afsus|/rɪˈɡret/|express regret','prevent|oldini olmoq|/prɪˈvent/|prevent a delay'],read:'Our group missed the early bus because we used an old timetable. If we had checked the current timetable, we would have noticed the change. It is tempting to say that checking would have made the whole trip successful. That is less certain: heavy rain later closed the walking route. The mistake caused one delay, but it was not the only difficulty. During the review, the group separates facts from imagined alternatives. We know that the bus time changed. We can reasonably say that checking might have prevented the first delay. We cannot claim that it would have prevented the rain. This distinction makes the review useful rather than an exercise in blame. Next time, one person will verify transport information and another will check whether the route is open.',rq:[['Nimani ishonchli aytish mumkin?','checking could have prevented the first delay','checking would have stopped the rain','the old timetable was correct','Birinchi kechikish manbasi ma’lum.'],['Review maqsadi?','learn without oversimplifying blame','prove weather was controlled','cancel every trip','Sabablar ajratiladi.']],listen:'We missed the bus because the timetable was old. If we had checked, we might have avoided that delay. But the route later closed because of rain. Better planning would not have controlled the weather, so we should not blame one person for the whole outcome.',lq:[['Nima eski edi?','the timetable','the bus','the route','Old timetable.'],['Nima nazoratda emas?','the weather','checking information','sharing tasks','Ob-havo nazoratdan tashqari.']],table:[['Birinchi sabab','old timetable'],['Keyingi to‘siq','rain']],fill:[['If we had ___, we would have noticed. (check)','checked'],['We would have ___ earlier. (arrive)','arrived'],['If I ___ asked, she might have helped.','had']],fix:['If we would have checked, we would have noticed.','If we had checked, we would have noticed.'],mc:['Ehtiyotkor muqobil xulosa?','Checking might have prevented the delay.','Checking would have stopped the rain.','The delay never happened.','Might cheklangan ehtimol.'],task:'O‘tmishdagi muvaffaqiyatsiz reja haqida review: fakt, muqobil natija va ikki kelgusi amal.',model:'Our trip was delayed because we used an old timetable. If we had checked the current version, we would have noticed the earlier departure. This might have prevented the first delay. However, it would not have kept the walking route open during the rain. We should therefore avoid treating one mistake as the cause of every problem. For the next trip, one person will verify transport information on the day before departure, while another will check the route conditions. The purpose of this review is to improve decisions, rather than simply identify someone to blame for an outcome affected by several factors.',speak:'Sherigingizning o‘tmish haqidagi haddan tashqari qat’iy xulosasini muloyim tuzating.',transform:['Third conditional: We did not check, so we did not notice.','If we had checked, we would have noticed.'],structure:['The timetable caused the first delay.','Rain later closed the route.','One better decision would not have controlled every outcome.']}),
advanced('B2',4,{t:'Mixed Conditional: o‘tmish va hozir',goal:'O‘tgan qarorning hozirgi oqibatini aniq vaqt aloqasi bilan ifodalaysiz.',context:'Ko‘nikma o‘rganishga kech boshlagan ishtirokchi.',rules:['If + had + V3, would + V hozirgi natijaga ulanadi: If I had practised, I would be more confident now.','If + past simple, would have + V3 doimiy yoki hozirgi holatning o‘tgan natijaga ta’sirini bildirishi mumkin.','Natija vaqtini now yoki yesterday bilan tekshiring; qolipni vaqt ma’nosiz aralashtirmang.'],pattern:'past choice → present result: had practised / would feel now',ex:['If I had practised earlier, I would feel more confident now.','If she knew the software, she would have helped yesterday.','We would be ready now if we had started sooner.','If I were more organised, I would have found the file.','He would not be tired now if he had slept longer.','If we had saved the data, we would have it today.'],v:['confidence|ishonch|/ˈkɒnfɪdəns/|build confidence','consequence|oqibat|/ˈkɒnsɪkwəns/|a present consequence','preparation|tayyorgarlik|/ˌprepəˈreɪʃən/|earlier preparation','adjust|moslashtirmoq|/əˈdʒʌst/|adjust a plan'],read:'Lola joined the presentation team only last week. She understands the topic but feels nervous using the software. If she had practised earlier, she would feel more confident now. This does not mean that she cannot contribute. Another student knows the software well but struggles to explain ideas clearly. Their skills are different, so the group changes the plan: Lola explains the argument while her partner operates the slides. The review connects past preparation to present confidence without turning confidence into a fixed personal quality. The group also plans short practice sessions for the next meeting. If preparation had begun earlier, today’s rehearsal would be easier; since it did not, they can still make useful choices now. A mixed conditional helps describe the time connection, but a practical plan must follow it.',rq:[['Hozirgi muammo nima?','confidence with software','no knowledge of the topic','no partner','Topic tushunarli, dasturda ishonch kam.'],['Guruh qanday yechim topdi?','divide roles according to skills','exclude Lola','avoid practice forever','Rollar turli ko‘nikmalarga mos.']],listen:'If Lola had practised the software earlier, she would feel more confident now. But she explains ideas clearly, so she will present while her partner handles the slides. We will also arrange short practice sessions for next week.',lq:[['Slaydni kim boshqaradi?','her partner','no one','Lola only','Partner handles slides.'],['Kelgusi yechim?','short practice sessions','stop presenting','buy new software only','Practice sessions.']],table:[['Lola vazifasi','present'],['Mashq muddati','next week']],fill:[['If I had practised, I would ___ confident now. (feel)','feel'],['If she ___ the software, she would have helped yesterday. (know)','knew'],['We would be ready now if we ___ started sooner.','had']],fix:['If I had practised, I would have feel confident now.','If I had practised, I would feel confident now.'],mc:['O‘tmishdan hozirga bog‘lanish?','If we had saved it, we would have it today.','If we save it, we will have it tomorrow.','We saved it yesterday.','Had saved → would have today.'],task:'Bir o‘tgan qarorning hozirgi oqibatini va hozir qilish mumkin bo‘lgan amallarni yozing.',model:'If I had practised the presentation software earlier, I would feel more confident now. However, I understand the topic and can explain the main argument clearly. Our group has therefore divided the tasks according to our strengths. I will present the ideas while my partner handles the slides. This arrangement solves the immediate problem, but it should not replace learning the missing skill. We will hold two short practice sessions before the next meeting. The past decision cannot be changed; the present plan can. I want our review to explain the consequence accurately without treating a temporary difficulty as a permanent weakness.',speak:'Hozirgi muammoni o‘tmish sababiga bog‘lang, so‘ng amaliy yechim taklif qiling.',transform:['Now natija bilan birlashtiring: I did not practise earlier. I am not confident now.','If I had practised earlier, I would be confident now.'],structure:['Earlier preparation affects confidence now.','Lola can still explain the topic.','The team can adjust roles and practise.'],visual:'timeline'}),
advanced('B2',5,{t:'Wish va if only',goal:'Hozirgi afsus, o‘tmishdagi afsus va o‘zgarish istagini ajratasiz.',context:'Klub xonasidagi shovqin va reja.',rules:['Wish + past simple hozirgi boshqa holat istagi: I wish the room were quieter.','Wish + had + V3 o‘tgan ishga afsus: I wish we had booked earlier.','Wish + would boshqa odamning o‘zgarishi kutilgan xatti-harakatiga; oddiy o‘z qobiliyatingiz uchun could yoki past shakli.'],pattern:'wish were / wish had booked / wish would stop',ex:['I wish the room were quieter.','I wish we had booked earlier.','I wish they would lower the music.','If only I could hear the speaker.','She wishes she had checked the date.','I wish I knew another place.'],v:['disturb|bezovta qilmoq|/dɪˈstɜːb/|disturb a meeting','regret|afsus|/rɪˈɡret/|regret a decision','considerate|e’tiborli|/kənˈsɪdərət/|a considerate neighbour','request|so‘rov|/rɪˈkwest/|make a request'],read:'Our club booked a small room for a discussion, but loud music from the next room made conversation difficult. Several students said they wished the room were quieter. The organiser wished she had checked the programme before booking. Another student said he wished the neighbours would lower the music. These sentences express different wishes, yet none is a direct request to the people who can help. The group therefore speaks to the venue manager and asks whether another room is available. The manager offers a quieter space for the final half of the meeting. The students still lose some time, but they learn to separate regret from action. Wishing describes dissatisfaction; a respectful request can change the situation. At the next booking, they will ask about nearby activities rather than assume the room is quiet.',rq:[['Nega wish yetarli emas?','it does not directly request a change','it guarantees a new room','it changes the past','Wish istak, harakat uchun so‘rov kerak.'],['Qaysi o‘tgan qaror afsus?','not checking the programme','lowering the music','moving to a quiet room','Had checked o‘tmish.']],listen:'I wish we had checked the programme before booking. The music is too loud. I wish they would lower it, but we should ask the manager for help. There is a quieter room available for the second half of our meeting.',lq:[['Yangi xona qachon?','the second half','next year','the first five minutes','Second half.'],['Kimdan yordam?','the manager','the bus driver','nobody','Ask manager.']],table:[['Muammo','loud music'],['Yechim','a quieter room']],fill:[['I wish we ___ checked earlier.','had'],['I wish they ___ lower the music.','would'],['If only I ___ hear the speaker.','could']],fix:['I wish I would know another place.','I wish I knew another place.'],mc:['O‘tgan afsus qaysi?','I wish we had booked earlier.','I wish it were quieter.','I wish they would stop.','Had booked o‘tmish.'],task:'Shikoyat emailida muammo, afsus va so‘rovni aralashtirmasdan yozing.',model:'Dear manager, our club booked the room for a discussion, but loud music from the next room made it difficult to hear one another. I wish we had checked the programme before booking. However, we were not told that a noisy event would take place nearby. Thank you for offering a quieter room for the second half of our meeting. For future bookings, could you please provide information about other activities in the building? This would help groups choose a suitable space. We understand that different events have different needs, and we would appreciate a clear way to plan around them.',speak:'Afsusni ayting, keyin hurmat bilan yordam so‘rang.',transform:['O‘tgan afsus: We did not check the programme.','I wish we had checked the programme.'],structure:['The room was too noisy for discussion.','A quieter room was available later.','Future bookings need clearer information.']}),
advanced('B2',6,{t:'Would rather va had better',goal:'Afzallikni ogohlantirishdan ajratib, mos ohangda tavsiya berasiz.',context:'Taqdimot oldidagi ikki tanlov.',rules:['Would rather + V afzallik; boshqa ega bilan would rather + subject + past simple.','Had better + V vaziyatga bog‘liq kuchli maslahat; salbiy oqibat ehtimoli bor.','Had better not; would rather not. Had better o‘tgan zamon emas va would rather bilan bir xil kuchda emas.'],pattern:'would rather practise / would rather you checked / had better save',ex:['I would rather practise now.','I would rather you checked the slides.','We had better save a copy.','You had better not rely on one computer.','She would rather not speak first.','Would you rather work in pairs?'],v:['backup|zaxira nusxa|/ˈbækʌp/|keep a backup','preference|afzallik|/ˈprefərəns/|express a preference','warning|ogohlantirish|/ˈwɔːnɪŋ/|a practical warning','rely on|tayanmoq|/rɪˈlaɪ ɒn/|rely on one device'],read:'Before the school presentation, two students discuss how to use the final twenty minutes. One would rather practise speaking; the other prefers checking the slides. Both activities are useful, and neither preference is a rule. A teacher then notices that the only copy of the presentation is on one computer. She says they had better save a backup because a technical problem could stop the talk. This advice has a stronger practical reason than either student’s preference. The group divides the time: one checks the slides while the other rehearses, and they save an extra copy first. The conversation works because they explain the purpose behind each suggestion. Treating every preference as a warning would create unnecessary pressure. Treating a real risk as a minor preference could leave the group unprepared.',rq:[['Nima kuchli maslahatga sabab?','only one copy could be lost','one student dislikes speaking','slides are always wrong','Zaxirasiz texnik xavf.'],['Rollar qanday bo‘lindi?','check and rehearse in parallel','do nothing','only discuss preferences','Ikkala foydali ish.']],listen:'I would rather practise the talk now. Could you check the slides? Before we do either task, we had better save a backup. There is only one copy, and we should not rely on one computer.',lq:[['Avval nima?','save a backup','cancel the talk','buy a computer','Before either task backup.'],['Kim slaydni tekshirsin?','the listener','the entire audience','nobody','Could you.']],table:[['Birinchi xavf yechimi','backup'],['Afzallik','practise the talk']],fill:[['I would rather ___ now. (practise)','practise'],['I would rather you ___ the slides. (check)','checked'],['We had better not ___ on one device. (rely)','rely']],fix:['We had better to save a copy.','We had better save a copy.'],mc:['Kuchli vaziyatli maslahat?','You had better save a backup.','I would rather sit here.','I prefer blue.','Risk sababli had better.'],task:'Ikki afzallik va bitta zarur ogohlantirish bilan hamkorlik rejasini yozing.',model:'We have twenty minutes before the presentation. I would rather practise the explanation, while my partner would prefer to check the slides. Both tasks support the same aim, so we can work in parallel instead of arguing about which one is more useful. First, we had better save a backup because the presentation is currently stored on only one computer. If that device fails, our preferences will no longer matter. Once the copy is safe, we can use ten minutes for preparation and ten for a joint rehearsal. This plan respects individual preferences while dealing with the most important risk first.',speak:'Sherik bilan ikki variantdan birini kelishib tanlang; maslahat kuchini asoslang.',transform:['Boshqa ega bilan afzallik: Please check the slides; that is my preference.','I would rather you checked the slides.'],structure:['Two preferences serve the same aim.','One missing backup creates a serious risk.','Deal with the risk, then divide the tasks.']})
 ,
brief('B2',7,{t:'Past modals: dalil, ehtimol va tanqid',goal:'Must have, might have va should have bilan turli ishonchni ko‘rsatasiz.',rules:'Must have + V3 kuchli xulosa, might have ehtimol.|Can’t have dalilga zid natijani rad etadi; should have o‘tgan maslahat yoki tanqid.|Didn’t need to bilan needn’t have done bir xil emas: ikkinchisida ish bajarilgan.',pattern:'must have / might have / should have + V3',ex:['She must have left early.','They might have taken another bus.','He cannot have read the final version.','We should have checked the address.','You need not have printed two copies.','The message may have gone to spam.'],v:'assumption|taxmin|/əˈsʌmpʃən/|question an assumption;plausible|ishonarli|/ˈplɔːzəbəl/|a plausible explanation;verify|tekshirmoq|/ˈverɪfaɪ/|verify an address;oversight|e’tiborsizlik|/ˈəʊvəsaɪt/|a small oversight',read:'The speaker has not arrived, although the meeting began ten minutes ago. One student says she must have forgotten. Another suggests that she might have taken the wrong bus. Neither has spoken to her, so the first explanation is stronger than the evidence allows. The organiser checks the invitation and finds an old address. They should have verified it before sending. The speaker then calls from the other building. This confirms one explanation but does not justify blaming her for forgetting. Reviewing the language matters: a possibility should not become a fact just because it is repeated confidently. The next invitation will include a map and a contact number.',question:['Avvalgi qat’iy xulosa muammosi?','it exceeded the evidence','it was confirmed immediately','it had no grammar','Dalilsiz must have juda qat’iy.'],inference:['Old address nimani tushuntiradi?','why she went elsewhere','why she dislikes meetings','why buses stopped','Keyingi telefon xabari joyni tasdiqlaydi.'],keyword:'address',responseKey:'verification',response:'We should verify information before blaming someone.',fill:[['She might have ___ another bus. (take)','taken'],['We should have ___ the address. (check)','checked'],['He cannot ___ read the new version.','have']],fix:['She must has forgotten.','She must have forgotten.'],transform:['Ehtimol sifatida: Perhaps she took another bus.','She might have taken another bus.'],task:'Kechikish haqidagi emailda fakt, ehtimol va yaxshilash tavsiyasini ajrating.',model:'We know that the speaker arrived at the old building. Before her call, we only had possible explanations for the delay. She might have taken the wrong bus, but there was no evidence that she had forgotten the meeting. We should have checked the invitation address before sending it. For the next event, please verify the location and include a contact number. This will reduce confusion and help us respond without blaming someone on the basis of an assumption.',structure:['The cause was initially uncertain.','The invitation contained an old address.','Verify details before drawing conclusions.']}),
brief('B2',8,{t:'Passive: jarayonni markazga qo‘yish',goal:'Murakkab passive zamonlarini hisobot maqsadiga mos qo‘llaysiz.',rules:'Passive be + V3; zamon va aspect be shakliga o‘tadi.|Has been repaired — tugallangan natija; is being repaired — davom etayotgan ish.|Agent muhim bo‘lsa by bilan ayting; mas’uliyatni yashirish uchun passive tanlamang.',pattern:'is being checked / has been checked / will be checked',ex:['The roof is being repaired.','The main room has been inspected.','The remaining windows will be checked.','The report was written by the engineer.','The building had been closed before the visit.','Safety rules must be followed.'],v:'inspect|tekshirmoq|/ɪnˈspekt/|inspect a building;responsibility|mas’uliyat|/rɪˌspɒnsəˈbɪləti/|take responsibility;maintenance|texnik qarov|/ˈmeɪntənəns/|regular maintenance;agent|bajaruvchi|/ˈeɪdʒənt/|name the agent',read:'The sports hall has been inspected, and the roof is being repaired. A public notice says that the remaining windows will be checked before reopening. Passive forms keep attention on the building and the sequence of work. However, the notice also says that a mistake was made without naming who will correct it. Parents ask for a contact person, not because every sentence needs an agent, but because someone must answer questions. The manager adds the maintenance team’s name and a review date. An effective report can focus on processes while still making responsibility clear. Avoiding an agent is reasonable when the person is unknown or irrelevant; it is less helpful when readers need to know who can act.',question:['Passive nima uchun foydali?','it focuses on the work sequence','it proves nobody is responsible','it removes every agent','Jarayon markazda.'],inference:['Parents nega kontakt so‘radi?','they needed someone who could act','they wanted grammar rules','all repairs were finished','Mas’uliyat amaliy muhim.'],keyword:'maintenance',responseKey:'responsibility',response:'Readers need a clear contact as well as a process description.',fill:[['The roof is being ___. (repair)','repaired'],['The room has ___ inspected.','been'],['Rules must be ___. (follow)','followed']],fix:['The roof is being repair.','The roof is being repaired.'],transform:['Passive: The engineer has inspected the hall.','The hall has been inspected by the engineer.'],task:'Ta’mirlash hisobotida ish holati va mas’ul aloqani aniq yozing.',model:'The hall has been inspected, and the roof is being repaired by the maintenance team. The remaining windows will be checked before the hall reopens. The process is not yet complete, so students should continue using the smaller room. Questions can be sent to the building manager, who will publish a new review date on Friday. This report focuses on work completed and work in progress while giving readers a clear contact. A process description should not leave responsibility unclear.',structure:['The hall is not ready to reopen.','Inspection is complete, but repairs continue.','Name the contact and the next review date.']}),
brief('B2',9,{t:'Reporting passive',goal:'Xabar manbasini faktning o‘zidan ajratib ko‘rsatasiz.',rules:'It is reported that … va X is reported to … manba xabarini bildiradi.|Oldingi voqea uchun to have + V3: is said to have moved.|Reported xabar tasdiqlangan degani emas; manba va cheklovni ko‘rsating.',pattern:'It is reported that / is believed to have',ex:['It is reported that the centre will reopen.','The centre is expected to reopen in May.','The organiser is said to have changed the plan.','The figures are believed to be incomplete.','It was announced that entry would be free.','The team is thought to have consulted residents.'],v:'reportedly|xabarlarga ko‘ra|/rɪˈpɔːtɪdli/|reportedly reopened;source|manba|/sɔːs/|a named source;confirm|tasdiqlamoq|/kənˈfɜːm/|confirm a date;rumour|mish-mish|/ˈruːmə/|an unconfirmed rumour',read:'It is reported that the community centre will reopen in May. A local article names the manager as its source, but an online post repeats the claim without that detail. The centre is also said to have changed its entry rules. No official notice confirms the rules yet. Students compare the reports and find that the reopening date comes from one interview, while the rule change began as an unnamed comment. Reporting passive is useful because it signals that information is attributed to someone. It does not show whether the source is reliable. Before publishing their own summary, the students contact the centre and label the unconfirmed detail clearly. A careful summary distinguishes a reported plan from a completed or guaranteed event.',question:['Reopening date manbasi?','one interview with the manager','a completed reopening','several independent reports','Maqola bitta interviewga tayangan.'],inference:['Reporting passive nimani kafolatlamaydi?','source reliability','attribution','a reporting structure','Ishonchlilikni alohida tekshirish kerak.'],keyword:'source',responseKey:'confirmation',response:'Attribution is useful, but unconfirmed rules need checking.',fill:[['The centre is expected ___ reopen.','to'],['The plan is said to have ___. (change)','changed'],['It is ___ that entry will be free. (report)','reported']],fix:['The centre is said have changed its rules.','The centre is said to have changed its rules.'],transform:['Reporting passive: People believe the figures are incomplete.','The figures are believed to be incomplete.'],task:'Ikki xabarni tekshirib, tasdiqlangan va taxminiy qismlar ajratilgan yangilik summarysi yozing.',model:'The centre is expected to reopen in May, according to an interview with its manager. This is a reported plan, rather than evidence that the building has already reopened. A separate claim about entry rules remains unconfirmed. The online post repeating it does not name an original source. We recommend checking the centre’s official notice before making travel plans. Our summary therefore keeps the reopening report and the uncertain rule change separate, so that readers can judge how strongly each detail is supported.',structure:['A report announces a reopening plan.','The rule change lacks a named source.','Separate reported plans from confirmed events.']}),
brief('B2',10,{t:'Causative have va get',goal:'Xizmatni o‘zi bajarish va boshqaga bajartirishni farqlaysiz.',rules:'Have/get + object + V3: I had my laptop repaired — xizmatni boshqa odam bajargan.|Have someone do va get someone to do odamni bajarishga jalb qiladi.|Had something stolen kutilmagan boshdan kechirilgan holat bo‘lishi mumkin; buyurtma degani emas.',pattern:'have a device repaired / get someone to check it',ex:['I had my laptop repaired.','We got the printer checked.','She had a technician install the update.','I got my brother to test the microphone.','He had his bag stolen on the bus.','Will you have the report printed?'],v:'technician|texnik mutaxassis|/tekˈnɪʃən/|a qualified technician;service|xizmat|/ˈsɜːvɪs/|book a service;arrange|tashkil qilmoq|/əˈreɪndʒ/|arrange a repair;warranty|kafolat|/ˈwɒrənti/|check the warranty',read:'The club printer stopped working before a display was due. Ali said he had repaired it, which sounded as if he had done the technical work himself. He actually had it repaired by a local technician. The distinction matters when the teacher asks who can explain the fault. Ali arranged the service but did not diagnose the machine. The club checks the warranty before paying and asks the technician for a short written record. Later, another student says she had her bag stolen on the bus. This has the same broad grammatical shape, but she did not arrange the action. Context determines whether the structure describes a service or an unwanted experience. Clear wording prevents mistaken assumptions about skills and responsibility.',question:['Ali aslida nima qilgan?','arranged a repair','diagnosed every fault himself','stole a bag','Had it repaired xizmat.'],inference:['Bag stolen nimani anglatadi?','an unwanted experience','a booked service','a repair request','Kontekst buyurtma emas.'],keyword:'service',responseKey:'context',response:'The same form can describe an arranged service or an unwanted experience.',fill:[['I had my laptop ___. (repair)','repaired'],['I got him ___ test the microphone.','to'],['She had a technician ___ the update. (install)','install']],fix:['I got him test the microphone.','I got him to test the microphone.'],transform:['Xizmat: A technician repaired my laptop for me.','I had my laptop repaired.'],task:'Ta’mir xizmatini so‘rash uchun muammo, muddat va kafolat haqidagi email yozing.',model:'Dear technician, our club would like to have its printer checked before Friday. It stopped working during a print job, and we have not tried to open it ourselves. Could you explain the likely inspection time and whether the service is covered by the warranty? We need a written record of any work carried out. I am arranging the repair on behalf of the club, so please contact me before replacing parts. This will help us understand the cost and keep responsibility clear.',structure:['The printer needs professional inspection.','The club must check warranty and cost.','Arrange the service and request a record.']}),
brief('B2',11,{t:'Reporting verbs va mas’uliyat',goal:'Deny, admit, suggest va warn qoliplarini ma’noga mos tanlaysiz.',rules:'Admit/deny + -ing; suggest + -ing yoki that-clause.|Warn someone not to; agree to; apologise for + -ing.|Reporting verb muallifning talqinini ham ko‘rsatadi: neutral said o‘rniga deny deyish uchun rad etish dalili kerak.',pattern:'admitted changing / denied sharing / warned us not to',ex:['She admitted changing the date.','He denied sharing the file.','They suggested checking the records.','The teacher warned us not to publish names.','I agreed to correct the notice.','She apologised for sending the wrong link.'],v:'admit|tan olmoq|/ədˈmɪt/|admit a mistake;deny|rad etmoq|/dɪˈnaɪ/|deny sharing;clarify|aniqlashtirmoq|/ˈklærɪfaɪ/|clarify a statement;account|bayon|/əˈkaʊnt/|a fair account',read:'A meeting summary said that one student admitted hiding a file. The student had only said that she moved it to another folder. The writer had chosen a reporting verb that added a judgement unsupported by the statement. After checking the recording, the group rewrote the sentence neutrally. Another student did apologise for sending the wrong link, so that verb was justified. The teacher warned everyone not to publish names before the facts were checked. Reporting verbs can make a summary concise, but they must preserve the speaker’s intention. A strong verb is not automatically a more accurate verb. The revised account separates acknowledged mistakes, suggestions, and disputed claims rather than turning all of them into confessions.',question:['Birinchi summary xatosi?','the verb added unsupported judgement','it was too neutral','the file never existed','Admitted hiding aytilmagan talqin.'],inference:['Qaysi verb asoslangan?','apologised for sending the wrong link','admitted hiding','confessed stealing','U haqiqatan uzr so‘ragan.'],keyword:'account',responseKey:'accuracy',response:'The summary needs accuracy rather than the strongest possible verb.',fill:[['She admitted ___ the date. (change)','changing'],['He agreed ___ correct it.','to'],['She apologised for ___ it. (send)','sending']],fix:['They suggested to check the records.','They suggested checking the records.'],transform:['Reporting: “I changed the date,” she said, accepting responsibility.','She admitted changing the date.'],task:'Neytral bayon yozing; uch reporting verb uchun aniq aytilgan gapni dalil qiling.',model:'The group reviewed the file incident and corrected its first summary. Lola said she had moved the file; she did not admit hiding it. Ali apologised for sending the wrong link, and the teacher warned everyone not to publish names before checking the facts. The group suggested reviewing the recording and agreed to update the notice. These verbs represent different actions and should not be treated as interchangeable. A fair summary preserves what speakers accepted, disputed, or proposed without adding unsupported judgement.',structure:['The original verb distorted the statement.','The recording supports more neutral wording.','Preserve intention when reporting speech.']}),
brief('B2',12,{t:'Non-defining relative clauses',goal:'Qo‘shimcha izohni shaxsni aniqlovchi ma’lumotdan ajratasiz.',rules:'Non-defining clause vergul bilan ajratiladi va allaqachon aniqlangan obyektga qo‘shimcha ma’lumot beradi.|Bu yerda that ishlatilmaydi; relative pronoun odatda tashlanmaydi.|The students who arrived early va the students, who arrived early, turli guruh ma’nosini beradi.',pattern:'Lola, who leads the club, … / the hall, which opened last year, …',ex:['Lola, who leads the club, welcomed us.','The hall, which opened last year, is busy.','My neighbour, whose son studies here, helped.','The guide, whom we met yesterday, returned.','We visited Bukhara, where my aunt lives.','The printer stopped, which delayed the display.'],v:'additional|qo‘shimcha|/əˈdɪʃənəl/|additional information;identify|aniqlamoq|/aɪˈdentɪfaɪ/|identify a person;omit|tushirib qoldirmoq|/əˈmɪt/|omit a pronoun;distinction|farq|/dɪˈstɪŋkʃən/|a meaning distinction',read:'Two notices describe a club visit. One says that the students who arrived early helped arrange chairs. The other says that the students, who arrived early, helped arrange chairs. The first identifies a subgroup; the second adds information about the whole group already being discussed. A small punctuation change therefore changes the claim. Lola, who leads the club, asks the writer to check which meaning matches the attendance record. Only five students arrived early, so the first notice is accurate. The revised report also names the hall, which opened last year. That detail is interesting but not necessary to identify the hall in this context. Grammar helps readers distinguish essential identification from additional background, rather than simply making sentences longer.',question:['Birinchi notice kimlarni ajratadi?','the early-arriving subgroup','every student','the whole town','Defining clause kichik guruh.'],inference:['Record qaysi gapni asoslaydi?','the version without commas','the version with commas','neither because nobody arrived','Faqat beshta erta kelgan.'],keyword:'distinction',responseKey:'subgroup',response:'The attendance record supports a subgroup rather than a claim about everyone.',fill:[['Lola, ___ leads the club, welcomed us.','who'],['The hall, ___ opened last year, is busy.','which'],['My neighbour, ___ son studies here, helped.','whose']],fix:['Lola, that leads the club, welcomed us.','Lola, who leads the club, welcomed us.'],transform:['Qo‘shimcha clause: Lola leads the club. Lola welcomed us.','Lola, who leads the club, welcomed us.'],task:'Visit reportda bir defining va ikki non-defining clause ishlating; guruh chegarasini izohlang.',model:'The students who arrived early helped arrange the chairs. Only five students were present at that time, so the report should not imply that the whole group arrived early. Lola, who leads the club, checked the attendance record before publishing the notice. The visit took place in the hall, which opened last year. This detail provides background without identifying a different hall. Our wording separates the subgroup that performed the task from additional information about people and places already known to the reader.',structure:['Only a subgroup arrived early.','Five students appear in the record.','Use defining information to identify that subgroup.']}),
brief('B2',13,{t:'Reduced relative va participle clauses',goal:'Qisqartirilgan gaplarda bajaruvchi mosligini tekshirasiz.',rules:'Students waiting outside = students who are waiting; books written recently passive ma’no.|Having checked the list, we … avvalgi amal, asosiy gap egasi bir xil bo‘lishi kerak.|Dangling participle: Walking home, the rain began — yomg‘ir yurmagan; egani tuzating.',pattern:'waiting outside / written recently / having checked',ex:['Students waiting outside need tickets.','The reports written yesterday are ready.','Having checked the list, we opened the door.','Walking home, I noticed the rain.','Built last year, the hall is modern.','Not knowing the answer, she asked for help.'],v:'reduce|qisqartirmoq|/rɪˈdjuːs/|reduce a clause;subject|ega|/ˈsʌbdʒɪkt/|a shared subject;sequence|ketma-ketlik|/ˈsiːkwəns/|an action sequence;ambiguity|noaniqlik|/ˌæmbɪˈɡjuːəti/|avoid ambiguity',read:'A student tries to make a report shorter: “Entering the hall, the lights were bright.” The sentence seems to make the lights enter the hall. She changes it to “Entering the hall, I noticed the bright lights.” The action now has a clear subject. Another sentence describes reports written yesterday; here the reports receive the action, so the past participle is appropriate. Concision can make a report easier to read, but it is useful only when the relation between actions stays clear. The editor checks each shortened clause by expanding it. If the expanded version names a different subject or changes active to passive meaning, the shortening needs revision. Saving a few words is not worth making readers guess who did what.',question:['Birinchi gapda muammo?','the implied subject is wrong','all participles are banned','lights are never bright','Kirayotgan ega noto‘g‘ri.'],inference:['Qisqartirishni qanday tekshiradi?','expand the clause and compare meaning','delete all subjects','count words only','Expanded clause aloqa tekshiruvi.'],keyword:'subject',responseKey:'clarity',response:'A shorter sentence is useful only when its subject remains clear.',fill:[['Students ___ outside need tickets. (wait)','waiting'],['Reports ___ yesterday are ready. (write)','written'],['Having ___ the list, we opened the door. (check)','checked']],fix:['Walking home, the rain began.','Walking home, I noticed that the rain began.'],transform:['Qisqartiring: Students who are waiting outside need tickets.','Students waiting outside need tickets.'],task:'Reportning uch gapini qisqartirib, ega va active/passive ma’nosini izohlang.',model:'Having checked the attendance list, we opened the hall to visitors. Students waiting outside were given tickets in order of arrival. The reports written yesterday were displayed near the entrance. These shortened clauses reduce repetition while keeping the actions clear. In the first sentence, we both checked the list and opened the hall. In the second, students do the waiting. In the third, reports receive the writing action. When editing, I expanded each clause to make sure the shorter version preserved the original meaning.',structure:['Concision must preserve the subject.','Expanding the clause reveals who acts.','Shorten only when meaning remains clear.']}),
brief('B2',14,{t:'Gerund va infinitive: ma’no o‘zgarishi',goal:'Remember, stop va try bilan shaklning ma’noga ta’sirini tushuntirasiz.',rules:'Remember doing — o‘tgan ish xotirasi; remember to do — bajarishni unutmaslik.|Stop doing — faoliyatni to‘xtatish; stop to do — boshqa ishni bajarish uchun to‘xtash.|Try doing — usulni sinash; try to do — harakat qilib bajarishga urinish.',pattern:'remember locking / remember to lock / stop to talk',ex:['I remember locking the door.','Please remember to lock the door.','We stopped talking.','We stopped to talk to the guide.','Try restarting the app.','I tried to open the heavy door.'],v:'attempt|urinish|/əˈtempt/|make an attempt;method|usul|/ˈmeθəd/|try a method;recall|eslamoq|/rɪˈkɔːl/|recall an action;interrupt|to‘xtatmoq|/ˌɪntəˈrʌpt/|interrupt an activity',read:'The club asks why a recorded interview contains a long pause. One student says they stopped talking; another says they stopped to talk to a guide outside. The first describes ending an activity, while the second gives the purpose of a pause in another activity. The organiser checks the timeline and finds that both happened at different points. A later note says, “Remember locking the equipment room.” This sounds like recalling an action, not asking someone to do it. The writer changes it to “Remember to lock the equipment room.” Small changes in verb patterns can affect instructions, not merely grammatical accuracy. When the group edits practical messages, it asks whether the sentence describes memory, intention, a method, or an attempt.',question:['Remember to lock nimani bildiradi?','a required future action','a memory of locking','proof of a locked door','To lock vazifani eslatadi.'],inference:['Ikki stop bayoni bir-biriga zidmi?','not necessarily, they refer to different points','always','both mean the same thing','Timeline turli nuqtalar.'],keyword:'method',responseKey:'meaning',response:'Verb patterns change what the instruction asks someone to do.',fill:[['Remember ___ lock the door.','to'],['I remember ___ the door. (lock)','locking'],['We stopped ___ talk to the guide.','to']],fix:['Please remember locking the room before you leave.','Please remember to lock the room before you leave.'],transform:['Xotira: I can recall that I locked the door.','I remember locking the door.'],task:'Amaliy yo‘riqnoma yozing, remember/stop/try juftliklarini ma’noda ajrating.',model:'Before leaving, please remember to lock the equipment room. If the recording app freezes, try restarting it before changing any settings. During an interview, stop talking when the speaker needs time to think. If you need to ask the guide a question, stop the recording to talk rather than recording an unrelated conversation. I remember checking the battery last time, but that memory does not guarantee it is charged today. These instructions distinguish future actions, possible methods, and memories of completed work.',structure:['Verb patterns encode different intentions.','Remembering an action differs from remembering to act.','Check the meaning, not just the ending.']}),
brief('B2',15,{t:'Articles va determiners: umumiydan aniqga',goal:'Umumiy guruh va ma’lum obyektni matn bo‘ylab izchil belgilaysiz.',rules:'A/an yangi sanaladigan birlik; the suhbatdan yoki vaziyatdan aniqlangan obyekt.|Ko‘plik va sanalmaydigan ot bilan umumiy ma’noda zero article: libraries, information.|Each/every birlik; both/all guruh; an tovushga qarab: an hour, a university.',pattern:'a proposal → the proposal / information / each student',ex:['We received a proposal.','The proposal needs more evidence.','Libraries provide information.','Each student has a role.','Both plans have advantages.','It takes an hour to reach a university.'],v:'reference|ishora|/ˈrefərəns/|clear reference;general|umumiy|/ˈdʒenərəl/|a general claim;specific|aniq|/spəˈsɪfɪk/|a specific object;determiner|aniqlovchi|/dɪˈtɜːmɪnə/|choose a determiner',read:'A student opens her report with a proposal for a reading corner. In the next sentence, the proposal refers to the same idea, so the definite article helps the reader follow it. She then writes that the libraries help children, although she means libraries in general rather than a known set. Removing the article makes the scope clearer. Her teacher also checks determiners: each student has a role, but both teams share one display. These choices are small, yet they tell readers whether the report describes one object, a known group, or a general category. The editor does not replace every article mechanically. She asks what the reader can already identify and whether the intended claim applies generally or specifically.',question:['Ikkinchi proposal nega the?','the reader can identify the earlier idea','every noun needs the','it begins with a consonant','Avvalgi a proposalga qaytadi.'],inference:['Umumiy libraries oldida nima?','no article','always the','always an','Umumiy ko‘plik zero article.'],keyword:'reference',responseKey:'scope',response:'Determiners help readers identify the scope of a claim.',fill:[['We received ___ proposal.','a'],['___ proposal needs evidence. (oldingi taklif)','The'],['Each student ___ a role. (have)','has']],fix:['Each student have a role.','Each student has a role.'],transform:['Aniq oldingi obyekt: We received a proposal. This proposal needs evidence.','We received a proposal. The proposal needs evidence.'],task:'Taklif matnida a/the/zero article va each/both bilan reference xaritasini yozing.',model:'We have received a proposal for a reading corner. The proposal suggests using one quiet part of the library twice a week. Libraries provide information, but students also need space to discuss what they read. Each student would have a role in preparing the display, while both groups would share responsibility for keeping it tidy. This distinction matters: the report describes one particular proposal and one known library, while its claim about libraries and information is general. We recommend reviewing the proposal after a short trial.',structure:['Introduce one proposal.','Refer back to the same proposal.','Distinguish specific objects from general categories.']}),
brief('B2',16,{t:'Concession, purpose va result',goal:'Qarshi dalil, maqsad va oqibatni bog‘lovchi bilan aniq ajratasiz.',rules:'Although/even though + clause; despite/in spite of + noun yoki -ing.|So that + clause maqsad; so/such … that natija.|Despite of emas. Although va butni bitta asosiy juftlikda takrorlamang.',pattern:'although it is costly / despite the cost / so that / so useful that',ex:['Although the plan is costly, it may help.','Despite the cost, we support a trial.','We added labels so that visitors could navigate.','The room was so busy that we waited.','It was such a useful guide that we shared it.','Even though opinions differ, we can agree on a trial.'],v:'concession|yon beruvchi dalil|/kənˈseʃən/|make a concession;purpose|maqsad|/ˈpɜːpəs/|state a purpose;consequence|oqibat|/ˈkɒnsɪkwəns/|a likely consequence;trial|sinov|/ˈtraɪəl/|a limited trial',read:'The school considers extending library hours. Although the plan would cost money, supporters argue that students need a quiet place after lessons. Critics agree with the aim but question whether enough students would attend. The school proposes a two-week trial so that it can collect attendance data before making a permanent decision. Last year, a popular event was so busy that the room became difficult to use. That result does not prove every extended session will be crowded. A reasoned report separates the purpose of a trial from the consequence of a past event. It also acknowledges the cost without treating it as a complete argument against the plan. Shared aims can make disagreement more productive when the uncertain facts are tested.',question:['Trial maqsadi?','collect attendance evidence','prove every day is crowded','avoid every cost','So that maqsad.'],inference:['Critics nimaga rozi?','the need for a quiet place','all costs are irrelevant','every session will be busy','Aimga rozi, attendancega shubha.'],keyword:'trial',responseKey:'evidence',response:'A shared aim still needs evidence about likely attendance.',fill:[['___ the cost, we support a trial.','Despite'],['We added labels so ___ visitors could navigate.','that'],['It was ___ useful that we shared it.','so']],fix:['Despite of the cost, we support a trial.','Despite the cost, we support a trial.'],transform:['Despite bilan: Although the plan is costly, we support it.','Despite the cost, we support the plan.'],task:'Advantages/disadvantages matnida qarshi dalil, maqsad va natijani ajrating.',model:'Although longer library hours would cost money, they could provide a quiet place for students after lessons. Critics reasonably ask whether enough students would attend. We propose a two-week trial so that attendance can be measured before a permanent decision is made. The success of one crowded event should not be treated as proof that every session will be busy. Despite the uncertainty, a limited trial offers a practical way to compare the benefit with the cost. The aim is to test the plan, rather than win an argument through repetition.',structure:['Students need quiet space, but costs matter.','A short trial can collect attendance data.','Use the evidence to decide rather than assume.']}),
brief('B2',17,{t:'Odobli e’tiroz va hedging',goal:'Fikrni yumshatib, dalil kuchiga mos aniqlik bilan bahslashasiz.',rules:'May/might, tends to, appears to xulosa kuchini chegaralaydi.|I see your point, but … kelishilgan qismdan e’tirozga o‘tadi.|Hedging dalilsiz fikrni isbotlamaydi; juda ko‘p yumshatish ham ma’noni noaniq qilishi mumkin.',pattern:'appears to / may suggest / I see your point, but',ex:['The result appears to support the plan.','This may suggest a useful pattern.','I see your point, but the sample is small.','The method tends to work better with clear instructions.','Could we consider another explanation?','I am not convinced that cost alone decides it.'],v:'sample|namuna|/ˈsɑːmpəl/|a small sample;tentative|dastlabki|/ˈtentətɪv/|a tentative conclusion;challenge|shubha ostiga qo‘ymoq|/ˈtʃælɪndʒ/|challenge a claim;courteous|hurmatli|/ˈkɜːtiəs/|a courteous disagreement',read:'A survey of eight volunteers finds that most prefer the new reading corner. The organiser announces that all students clearly support it. Another student agrees that the result is encouraging but points out that the sample is small and voluntary. She says the findings may suggest a useful pattern, not prove a school-wide preference. This wording limits the claim to what the evidence supports. Her objection is courteous because she recognises the useful work already done and proposes a larger survey. Hedging is not an excuse to avoid taking a position. The student still recommends keeping the corner during the trial. She simply separates a practical recommendation from a certainty the survey cannot establish.',question:['Survey nega umumiy xulosaga yetmaydi?','the sample is small and voluntary','eight is always zero','no one answered','Kichik o‘z ixtiyoriy tanlov.'],inference:['Student qanday pozitsiya oladi?','keep the trial while gathering better evidence','close immediately','claim certainty','Tavsiyasi aniq, xulosasi cheklangan.'],keyword:'sample',responseKey:'tentative',response:'The result is encouraging, but the conclusion should remain tentative.',fill:[['The result appears ___ support the plan.','to'],['This ___ suggest a pattern. (ehtimol)','may'],['I see your point, ___ the sample is small.','but']],fix:['Eight volunteers prove that every student agrees.','Eight volunteers suggest support, but do not prove that every student agrees.'],transform:['Ehtiyotkor qiling: The findings prove the plan works.','The findings may suggest that the plan works.'],task:'Kichik surveyga asoslangan xulosani cheklov va amaliy tavsiya bilan yozing.',model:'The survey result is encouraging: most of the eight volunteers preferred the reading corner. However, the sample is too small and selective to establish the view of all students. I recommend keeping the corner during the trial while collecting responses from a broader group. This position recognises the benefit already observed without claiming more than the evidence supports. I see the organiser’s point about enthusiasm, but we should distinguish support among volunteers from school-wide demand. A larger survey could help decide whether the arrangement should become permanent.',structure:['The early result is encouraging.','Only eight volunteers answered.','Keep the trial and gather broader evidence.']}),
brief('B2',18,{t:'Register: formal email va samimiy xabar',goal:'Bitta maqsadni auditoriyaga mos ikki uslubda ifodalaysiz.',rules:'Formal register aniq maqsad, hurmatli murojaat va mos so‘rov; murakkab so‘z shart emas.|Could you please … va I would appreciate … so‘rovni yumshatadi.|Informal qisqartma do‘stga mos; rasmiy xabarda haqorat yoki haddan tashqari talab ohangidan saqlaning.',pattern:'Could you please clarify …? / Can you tell me …?',ex:['Could you please clarify the deadline?','I would appreciate a written reply.','Please find the revised plan attached.','Can you tell me when it is due?','Thanks for checking this for me.','I am writing to request more information.'],v:'clarify|aniqlashtirmoq|/ˈklærɪfaɪ/|clarify a deadline;attached|ilova qilingan|/əˈtætʃt/|the attached plan;recipient|qabul qiluvchi|/rɪˈsɪpiənt/|a message recipient;tone|ohang|/təʊn/|a respectful tone',read:'Two emails ask for the same deadline. A message to a friend says, “Can you tell me when it is due?” A message to the school office says, “Could you please clarify the submission deadline?” The second is not better English in every situation; it suits a different relationship. A student initially writes a very long formal email with several vague phrases and no clear request. The teacher asks her to simplify it. She keeps a polite greeting, states the purpose, and asks one precise question. Register includes clarity as well as politeness. Choosing an audience does not require hiding meaning behind elaborate words. The office can answer more quickly because the revised message makes the requested action easy to identify.',question:['Ikkinchi xabar nega mos?','it suits the office relationship','it is always superior','it must be longer','Auditoriya register tanlaydi.'],inference:['Uzun email muammosi?','the request was unclear','it contained a greeting','it asked one precise question','Murakkablik aniqlikni yo‘qotgan.'],keyword:'recipient',responseKey:'clarity',response:'A formal request should remain easy to understand.',fill:[['Could you please ___ the deadline? (clarify)','clarify'],['I would appreciate ___ written reply.','a'],['Please find the plan ___. (attach)','attached']],fix:['Tell me the date now, office.','Could you please clarify the deadline?'],transform:['Formal qiling: Tell me when it is due.','Could you please clarify the deadline?'],task:'Bir so‘rovni do‘stga va maktab ofisiga mos ikki xabarda yozing.',model:'Dear school office, I am writing to ask about the deadline for submitting our club proposal. The notice gives the meeting date but does not state when proposals should arrive. Could you please clarify the submission deadline and confirm whether an electronic copy is acceptable? We would like to plan the final review before sending our work. I would appreciate a written reply so that I can share the information accurately with the group. Thank you for your help. Kind regards, Lola.',structure:['The recipient needs a clear request.','The notice omits the submission deadline.','Ask one precise question in a respectful tone.']}),
brief('B2',19,{t:'Word formation: so‘z oilalari',goal:'So‘zning vazifasiga ko‘ra noun, verb, adjective va adverb shaklini tanlaysiz.',rules:'Success noun, succeed verb, successful adjective, successfully adverb.|Prefix/suffix ma’no va so‘z turini o‘zgartirishi mumkin; har yangi shaklni lug‘atda tekshiring.|Negative prefixlar hamma so‘zga bir xil qo‘shilmaydi: possible/impossible, useful/useless.',pattern:'succeed → success → successful → successfully',ex:['The trial was successful.','The team completed it successfully.','Success depends on careful preparation.','They hope to succeed next time.','The instructions were useful.','The plan was impossible within one day.'],v:'successful|muvaffaqiyatli|/səkˈsesfəl/|a successful trial;successfully|muvaffaqiyat bilan|/səkˈsesfəli/|complete successfully;reliable|ishonchli|/rɪˈlaɪəbəl/|reliable evidence;reliability|ishonchlilik|/rɪˌlaɪəˈbɪləti/|check reliability',read:'The club report describes a successful trial, then claims that success proves the plan is reliable. The teacher asks what reliability means in this context. One positive event is evidence of success, but a reliable process should work consistently under similar conditions. The group repeats the trial with another class and checks whether the instructions can be followed without extra help. They also edit word forms. “The team worked successful” becomes “The team worked successfully.” Selecting the right suffix matters grammatically, while selecting the right concept matters logically. A word family can help express an idea precisely only when the writer understands the relation between the words. The revised report separates a successful event from evidence of reliability.',question:['Success nimani hali isbotlamaydi?','consistent reliability','a positive event','that the trial occurred','Bir muvaffaqiyat doimiylikni kafolatlamaydi.'],inference:['Successfully qanday ishlaydi?','it describes how they worked','it names an event','it describes a noun only','Adverb fe’lga.'],keyword:'reliability',responseKey:'consistency',response:'Reliability requires more than one successful event.',fill:[['The trial was ___. (success)','successful'],['They worked ___. (successful)','successfully'],['They hope to ___. (success)','succeed']],fix:['The team worked successful.','The team worked successfully.'],transform:['Adverb bilan: Their work was successful.','They worked successfully.'],task:'Trial reportda word family va success/reliability farqini qo‘llang.',model:'The first trial was successful, and the team completed the task successfully. However, one success does not establish the reliability of the process. We repeated the activity with another class to see whether the instructions could be followed without extra help. The second group also completed the task, although it needed more time. We therefore have encouraging evidence of consistency, but we should continue checking the method under similar conditions. The report uses different word forms to describe the result, the action, and the quality being evaluated.',structure:['The first trial succeeded.','A second group tested the same instructions.','Evaluate reliability across similar conditions.']}),
brief('B2',20,{t:'Collocations va phrasal verbs',goal:'Tabiiy birikmani vaziyat va so‘z tartibi bilan qo‘llaysiz.',rules:'Draw a conclusion, raise a concern, carry out a survey kabi birikmalarni kontekstda o‘rganing.|Put off — kechiktirmoq; carry out — bajarmoq; bring up — muhokamaga ko‘tarmoq.|Ajraladigan fe’lda olmosh o‘rtada: put it off; birikmani yodlash ma’noni tushunish o‘rnini bosmaydi.',pattern:'raise concerns / carry out a survey / put it off',ex:['We raised a concern about access.','The team carried out a survey.','Do not draw a conclusion too early.','They put the meeting off.','We should not put it off again.','She brought up another option.'],v:'raise a concern|tashvishni bildirmoq|/reɪz ə kənˈsɜːn/|raise a practical concern;carry out|bajarmoq|/ˈkæri aʊt/|carry out a survey;draw a conclusion|xulosa chiqarmoq|/drɔː ə kənˈkluːʒən/|draw a cautious conclusion;put off|kechiktirmoq|/pʊt ɒf/|put it off',read:'The committee put the meeting off because several students could not attend. A member then raised a concern that repeated delays might exclude people with limited free time. Another suggested carrying out a short survey before choosing a date. The group agreed, but one student drew a conclusion from only the first two replies. The organiser asked everyone to wait until the response period ended. Useful collocations make the minutes sound natural, yet they do not guarantee a sensible decision. The committee needs both accurate language and a fair process. In the revised minutes, it records the concern, the evidence to be collected, and the date when a conclusion will be discussed. This gives readers more than a list of fluent phrases.',question:['Nega first two replies yetarli emas?','the response period had not ended','all surveys are useless','there were no replies','Tanlov hali tugamagan.'],inference:['Minutes nima ko‘rsatishi kerak?','concern, evidence, and decision date','only fluent phrases','only the earliest replies','Jarayon qayd etiladi.'],keyword:'survey',responseKey:'fairness',response:'Natural phrasing should describe a fair process, not replace it.',fill:[['We ___ a concern. (raise)','raised'],['They carried ___ a survey.','out'],['Do not put ___ off. (it)','it']],fix:['Do not put off it again.','Do not put it off again.'],transform:['Phrasal verb: They postponed the meeting.','They put the meeting off.'],task:'Committee minutes: tashvish, survey, muddat va ehtiyotkor xulosa yozing.',model:'The committee raised a concern about repeated delays to the meeting. Some members have limited free time, so postponement may reduce their chance to participate. We agreed to carry out a short survey before choosing a new date. The response period will remain open until Friday, and we should not draw a conclusion from the earliest replies alone. At the next meeting, we will compare the full set of responses and explain how the chosen date balances different needs. These minutes record both the concern and the decision process.',structure:['Repeated postponement may exclude members.','A survey will collect wider availability.','Wait for the full response period before deciding.']}),
brief('B2',21,{t:'Opinion essay: dalil va qarshi fikr',goal:'Fikrni ikki dalil va adolatli counterargument bilan tuzasiz.',rules:'Opinion essay da’vosi aniq, paragraphs bir sababni rivojlantiradi.|Misolning da’voga qanday aloqasi borligini tushuntiring; faqat example sanamang.|Counterargumentni kuchsiz qilib ko‘rsatmang: uning asosli qismini tan olib javob bering.',pattern:'claim → evidence → explanation → counterargument → conclusion',ex:['I support a limited trial rather than an immediate change.','One reason is that the current evidence is incomplete.','For example, only volunteers answered.','Critics reasonably point out the cost.','However, a short trial can limit that cost.','The decision should follow the trial results.'],v:'claim|da’vo|/kleɪm/|support a claim;counterargument|qarshi dalil|/ˈkaʊntəˌɑːɡjʊmənt/|address a counterargument;justify|asoslamoq|/ˈdʒʌstɪfaɪ/|justify a recommendation;representative|vakillik qiluvchi|/ˌreprɪˈzentətɪv/|a representative sample',read:'Should the school replace every printed notice with an online message? Supporters say updates would reach readers quickly and reduce wasted paper. Critics point out that not every family checks the same app. A student essay initially describes critics as people who dislike technology. That weak version of their argument is easy to dismiss but does not address the access problem. The writer revises the essay to acknowledge the strongest objection and proposes a mixed trial: online messages plus one shared printed board. The trial would measure whether families receive important information on time. A persuasive essay should not merely defeat an imagined opponent. It should help readers compare realistic options and understand why a recommendation follows from the evidence.',question:['Criticsning asosiy dalili?','unequal access to the app','hatred of every technology','paper never costs money','Hamma bir appni tekshirmaydi.'],inference:['Revised essay kuchi nima?','it answers the strongest real objection','it ignores critics','it invents survey results','Accessga amaliy mixed yechim.'],keyword:'access',responseKey:'trial',response:'Test a mixed approach before removing the printed board.',fill:[['Critics reasonably ___ out the cost. (point)','point'],['A trial can ___ that cost. (limit)','limit'],['The decision should ___ the results. (follow)','follow']],fix:['Critics dislike technology, so their access concern is irrelevant.','Critics raise an access concern that the plan should address.'],transform:['Counterargumentni tan oling: Some families do not use the app.','Critics reasonably point out that some families do not use the app.'],task:'Online va printed notice haqida opinion essay: ikki dalil, real counterargument va tavsiya.',model:'I support testing online notices while keeping one shared printed board. Online messages can be updated quickly, which helps when an event changes at short notice. However, critics reasonably point out that some families do not check the same app. Removing every printed notice would therefore risk excluding them. A mixed trial could measure how reliably important information reaches families through each method. The aim should be timely access, rather than proving that one medium is always better. If the trial shows that online messages reach everyone, the school can reconsider the printed board with stronger evidence.',structure:['Access is more important than the medium.','Some families do not check the app.','Use a mixed trial to test reliable delivery.']}),
brief('B2',22,{t:'Report va review: maqsad farqi',goal:'Hisobotdagi kuzatuvni reviewdagi bahodan ajratasiz.',rules:'Report maqsad, dalil, natija va tavsiya; review tajriba va mezon asosidagi baho.|Baho subyektiv bo‘lsa uning mezonini ochiq ayting.|Sarlavhalar reportni skanerlashga yordam beradi; review ham faktni xolis saqlashi kerak.',pattern:'findings → recommendation / experience → evaluation',ex:['The report records attendance at each session.','The review evaluates the quality of the guide.','Most visitors found the labels clear.','The survey did not include evening visitors.','I would recommend the tour to first-time visitors.','The recommendation is limited to the evidence collected.'],v:'finding|aniqlangan natija|/ˈfaɪndɪŋ/|report findings;criterion|mezon|/kraɪˈtɪəriən/|an evaluation criterion;evaluate|baholamoq|/ɪˈvæljueɪt/|evaluate a guide;recommendation|tavsiya|/ˌrekəmenˈdeɪʃən/|a supported recommendation',read:'After a museum visit, the class writes two texts. The report records attendance and survey results for the organiser. The review helps future visitors decide whether the tour suits them. Both use the same experience, but they answer different questions. The report notes that the survey excluded evening visitors, so its findings are incomplete. The review explains that the guide’s clear explanations were useful for first-time visitors, although experienced visitors might want more detail. Neither text needs to pretend to be completely objective. It needs to show where facts end and evaluation begins. A recommendation becomes more useful when the reader knows the criteria and the audience for whom it was made.',question:['Report kimga ma’lumot beradi?','the organiser','only future tourists','nobody','Tashkilotchi natijalar uchun.'],inference:['Review nima bilan chegaralanadi?','the needs of its audience','word count alone','all visitors are identical','Birinchi marta keluvchilar uchun mos.'],keyword:'criterion',responseKey:'audience',response:'A recommendation is useful when readers know whom it suits.',fill:[['The review ___ the guide. (evaluate)','evaluates'],['Most visitors ___ the labels clear. (find, past)','found'],['The survey did not ___ evening visitors. (include)','include']],fix:['Every visitor will like it because I liked it.','I recommend it to first-time visitors because the explanations were clear.'],transform:['Mezonga bog‘lang: The tour was good.','The tour was useful for first-time visitors because the explanations were clear.'],task:'Bitta tashrif bo‘yicha qisqa report va review yozing; mezon va audience ni farqlang.',model:'The tour is a useful introduction for first-time visitors. The guide explains unfamiliar objects clearly and allows time for questions. I particularly valued the labels, which made it easy to return to an exhibit independently. However, visitors who already know the collection may want more detailed discussion. My recommendation is based on clarity and accessibility, rather than specialist depth. A separate attendance report should include the survey limitation: evening visitors were not asked for feedback. That limitation does not cancel the positive experience, but it narrows the claim we can make about all visitors.',structure:['The texts answer different questions.','Facts and evaluation share one experience.','State the criteria and limits of the recommendation.']}),
brief('B2',23,{t:'Formal complaint va request',goal:'Muammo, ta’sir va aniq yechimni dalil bilan so‘raysiz.',rules:'Complaint fakt va ta’sirni ajratadi; haqorat yechimga yordam bermaydi.|I would appreciate …, could you confirm … bilan so‘ralgan amal aniq bo‘lsin.|Muddat va dalilni ayting, lekin mavjud bo‘lmagan huquq yoki kafolatni o‘ylab topmang.',pattern:'problem → impact → evidence → requested action',ex:['I am writing about our booking.','The room was not available at the agreed time.','This delayed our meeting by thirty minutes.','The confirmation email gives a start time of ten.','Could you explain what caused the delay?','I would appreciate a clear response by Friday.'],v:'confirmation|tasdiq xabari|/ˌkɒnfəˈmeɪʃən/|booking confirmation;impact|ta’sir|/ˈɪmpækt/|describe the impact;resolution|yechim|/ˌrezəˈluːʃən/|seek a resolution;correspondence|yozishma|/ˌkɒrɪˈspɒndəns/|professional correspondence',read:'A club booking email confirms that the room will be available at ten. On the day, another group is still using it, and the club waits thirty minutes. The first complaint calls the venue dishonest. The writer cannot support that intention claim, so she revises it to state the observable problem and its effect. She attaches the confirmation and asks for an explanation and a practical solution for the next booking. The revised message is firm but respectful. It does not weaken the complaint; it makes the requested response easier to identify. Professional correspondence can express dissatisfaction without guessing someone’s motives. The most useful outcome is a clear arrangement that prevents the same delay, not simply a stronger adjective.',question:['Intention claim nega o‘zgartirildi?','dishonesty was not supported by evidence','there was no delay','politeness forbids complaints','Motiv dalili yo‘q.'],inference:['Revised complaint maqsadi?','a practical solution and explanation','stronger insults','hide the confirmation','Keyingi booking aniqligi.'],keyword:'confirmation',responseKey:'resolution',response:'A firm complaint should ask for a practical resolution.',fill:[['I am writing ___ our booking.','about'],['The delay ___ our meeting. (affect, past)','affected'],['Could you ___ the cause? (explain)','explain']],fix:['You are dishonest because our room was late.','The room was not available at the confirmed time, which delayed our meeting.'],transform:['Hurmatli request: Explain the delay.','Could you explain what caused the delay?'],task:'Booking complaint email: tekshiriladigan fakt, ta’sir, dalil va so‘ralgan yechim.',model:'Dear venue manager, I am writing about our booking for Tuesday at ten. The confirmation email gives that start time, but the room remained occupied until ten thirty. This delayed our meeting and reduced the time available for discussion. I have attached the confirmation for reference. Could you explain what caused the delay and confirm how the next booking will be protected from a similar problem? I would appreciate a clear response by Friday so that our group can plan its next session. Thank you for reviewing the matter.',structure:['A confirmed start time was missed.','The delay reduced discussion time.','Request an explanation and a practical prevention plan.']}),
brief('B2',24,{t:'Birgalikda qaror: B2 loyiha',goal:'Manbalarni qiyoslab, murosaga kelgan tavsiyani himoya qilasiz.',rules:'Bitta variantning foydasi boshqa ehtiyojni yo‘qqa chiqarmaydi.|Weigh up options, agree on criteria, reach a compromise suhbatni qarorga olib boradi.|Decision qayta ko‘riladigan mezon va muddat bilan mustahkamlanadi; dalilsiz qat’iylikdan saqlaning.',pattern:'compare criteria → weigh options → agree → review',ex:['We need to weigh up the options.','Could we agree on the main criteria?','The cheaper plan may exclude some users.','The flexible plan costs more but reaches more people.','Let us try a compromise for two weeks.','We will review the decision using attendance data.'],v:'weigh up|solishtirib baholamoq|/weɪ ʌp/|weigh up options;compromise|murosa|/ˈkɒmprəmaɪz/|reach a compromise;priority|ustuvorlik|/praɪˈɒrəti/|agree on priorities;feasible|amalga oshadigan|/ˈfiːzəbəl/|a feasible plan',read:'The school club has funds for one extra session each week. A survey favours a fixed afternoon, while interviews with students who travel far suggest that a rotating day would be fairer. The survey has more responses, but the interviews reveal a need the fixed schedule may overlook. The committee first agrees on three criteria: access, cost, and reliable staffing. It then compares the options against those criteria instead of choosing the most popular answer automatically. The group proposes alternating two afternoons for a short trial. This compromise may not satisfy every preference, but it can test whether more students attend without increasing the total number of sessions. The decision includes a review date and a way to collect evidence. Agreement is stronger when participants understand both the benefit and the remaining limitation.',question:['Interviews qanday yangi ehtiyojni ochdi?','access for students who travel far','a demand for no sessions','the exact staffing cost','Surveyda yo‘q access tafsiloti.'],inference:['Qaror nega review bilan?','the compromise still needs evidence','all uncertainty is gone','attendance never matters','Sinov natijasi tekshiriladi.'],keyword:'priority',responseKey:'compromise',response:'Agree on criteria before choosing the most popular option.',fill:[['We need to weigh ___ the options.','up'],['Could we agree ___ criteria?','on'],['We will ___ the decision. (review)','review']],fix:['More survey replies mean every other need is irrelevant.','More survey replies are useful, but other needs still require consideration.'],transform:['Murosa taklif qiling: We could test both afternoons.','Let us try a compromise using both afternoons.'],task:'B2 yakuniy loyiha: survey va interviewni qiyoslab committee report yozing, keyin qarorni og‘zaki himoya qiling.',model:'We recommend alternating two afternoons for a two-week trial. The survey favours a fixed day, but interviews show that students who travel far may need greater flexibility. We compared the options using access, cost, and staffing as criteria. Alternating days preserves one session per week while testing whether attendance becomes broader. This is a compromise, not proof that everyone will be satisfied. The committee should record attendance and ask students whether the change helps them participate. At the review meeting, we can retain, revise, or reject the arrangement based on evidence rather than preference alone.',structure:['Survey and interviews reveal different needs.','The committee agrees on shared criteria.','Test a compromise and review the evidence.']})
];
